   multiple usages of positron diffraction and core-level photoemission
   spectroscopy},
Journal = {PHYSICAL REVIEW MATERIALS},
Year = {2025},
Volume = {9},
Number = {1},
Month = {JAN 7},
Abstract = {The structure of an Al(111 )3 x 3-Si surface was examined by combining
   data from positron diffraction and core-level photoemission
   spectroscopy. Analysis of the diffraction rocking curves indicated that
   the overlayer had a flat honeycomb lattice structure. Simulations of Si
   core-level spectra calculated via the first principles indicated that
   one of the Si atoms in the unit cell was replaced by an Al atom. The
   surface superstructure was thus a two-dimensional layer of Al-embedded
   silicene on Al(111).},
